        "original_id": "fa89c0bf-33f9-5d27-bc39-7f82282a0536",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leucippus, Democritus\n- Organizations/Schools: Pluralist school, Atomists\n- Concepts: atomism, atoms\n\nFacts:\n- The Pluralist school is said to have included the Atomists, specifically Leucippus and Democritus.\n- Some ancient sources report that Leucippus was the earliest Greek philosopher to develop atomism.\n- Atomism is the idea that everything is composed entirely of imperishable, indivisible elements called atoms.\n- Leucippus often appears as the teacher of his pupil Democritus.\n- Democritus is also described as an originator of atomic theory.",
